  "subject": "Cross-spec coordination — bundle canonicalization ask for 5 Thingalog extension vars ready for Phase-2 promotion when the catdef cycle next opens. Per the project-bind two-phase pattern (express via .x- extension primitives now, canonicalize via catdef later), Thingalog has accumulated five .x-prefixed vars driven by real PO/Karen empirical need: .x-header_style (enum, catalog header treatment), .x-card_meta_fields (list of FieldDef refs, card-row meta line composition), .x-card_footer_field (FieldDef ref, card-row footer), .x-subtitle (text, catalog strapline — root-only, not subcat-inherited), .x-quick_filters (JSON array of {label, filter, sort?} — Saved Views, AI-curated via set_quick_filters MCP write). All renderer-read in production (builds ~500-540); two wired into _NON_INHERITED_ABOUT_KEYS (server.py:1293) for the right inheritance semantics. ASK: when cycle opens, promote .x-foo → .foo (recommend drop the prefix verbatim) + codify validator types in canonical schema + decide inheritance semantics + Director ratifies; Thingalog implementer does rename pass post-ratification. PLUS two substrate-shape FLAGS (not asks): (1) Saved Views as a reserved subcat (.views, sibling of .presets) — Thingalog's operational-metadata-as-reserved-subcats doctrine wants it eventually; current Thingalog disposition = DEFER (JSON-blob working, no concrete pain); re-trigger = sharing/export/permissions/versioning. (2) Unify Presets+Saved Views into one 'preset = {filter, sort, look}' bundle — substrate-shape question worth catdef awareness; current Thingalog = HOLD as siblings; both names carry semantic mass, future unification has migration cost; Thingalog will land on whichever shape catdef ratifies. Standard catdef cycle; no urgency; Thingalog substrate-hygiene Phase-1.5 (reporting + validation in list_themeable_variables keeping .x- prefix) lands now via implementer regardless of cycle timing.",

