  "body": "Per the project-bind two-phase pattern (feedback_photo_first_mental_model_invariant — express via existing primitives now, canonicalize via catdef-strategist later), Thingalog has accumulated FIVE .x-prefixed extension vars in production that are ready for canonical promotion when the catdef cycle next opens. Bundling so canonicalization happens as one coherent batch rather than five drip-feed requests. All five emerged from real PO/Karen empirical need (welch-arctic-collection chrome, magazine-flow catalog cards, the AI-curator-as-quick-filter-author Saved Views directive), not speculation. Phase-1 = .x- in production; Phase-1.5 = registration in list_themeable_variables reporting+validation (Thingalog implementer task, sibling memo); Phase-2 = canonical promotion (drop .x- prefix, codify validators in canonical schema). THE FIVE VARS: .x-header_style (enum, catalog header treatment / chrome variant per look-and-feel); .x-card_meta_fields (list of FieldDef refs, which fields appear in card-row meta line); .x-card_footer_field (FieldDef ref, single field in card-row footer); .x-subtitle (text, catalog description/strapline, root-catalog-only NOT inherited by subcats); .x-quick_filters (JSON array of {label, filter, sort?}, Saved Views — named one-click filter+sort bundles curated by AI peer via set_quick_filters MCP write). OPERATIONAL ANCHORS: all renderer-read in production (builds ~500-540); .x-subtitle + .x-quick_filters in _NON_INHERITED_ABOUT_KEYS (server.py:1293) for subcat-inheritance; each driven by concrete PO/Karen need + working Thingalog implementation across multiple catalogs. ASK: when catdef cycle next opens, promote five from .x-foo → .foo in canonical theme/preset vocab + standardize validator semantics in canonical schema (substrate-level point of canonicalization — other catdef-substrate implementations can use them). Specifically: (1) decide canonical names (recommend drop .x- prefix verbatim: .header_style, .card_meta_fields, .card_footer_field, .subtitle, .quick_filters; renameable if catdef wants different convention); (2) codify validator types (enum_membership for .header_style; list-of-FieldDef-refs for .card_meta_fields; single FieldDef ref for .card_footer_field; text for .subtitle; JSON-array-with-schema for .quick_filters); (3) decide inheritance semantics in canonical form (.subtitle + .quick_filters catalog-root-only in Thingalog — not subcat-inherited; other three follow normal theme-inheritance); (4) Director ratifies via standard cycle. Post-ratification: Thingalog implementer does rename pass (mechanical — .x-foo → .foo across _CATEGORY_BY_NAME, validators, renderer bindings, inheritance denylist). TWO SUBSTRATE-SHAPE CONCERNS (FLAGS, not asks for this cycle — awareness for catdef's longer-arc thinking): (1) SAVED VIEWS AS RESERVED SUBCAT? Thingalog Phase-1 stores .x-quick_filters as JSON blob on about catalog-root variable; feedback_operational_metadata_as_reserved_subcats doctrine ultimately wants Saved Views to live as items in a .views reserved subcat (same shape as Presets currently are items in .presets) — would give views CRUD + sharing + export + MCP parity with Presets for free; current Thingalog disposition = DEFER (JSON-blob working, no concrete pain); re-trigger = views need own sharing/export OR per-view permissions OR view-versioning. For catdef: if substrate eventually canonicalizes reserved-subcat patterns for operational metadata, .views is likely candidate alongside .presets (which already exists at substrate level via Thingalog PRESET_TEMPLATE). (2) UNIFY PRESETS + SAVED VIEWS INTO ONE 'preset = {filter, sort, look}' BUNDLE? Today Thingalog keeps Presets (visual look bundle, items in .presets) and Saved Views (filter+sort bundle, JSON in .x-quick_filters) as siblings; PO flagged eventual unification as possibility ('could we somehow combine the functionality of the filter bar and the presets?'); substrate-shape question = whether canonical 'Preset' concept should generalize to complete-catalog-state bundle (look ∪ filter ∪ sort) OR stay scoped to visual. Current Thingalog = HOLD as siblings; waits for forcing function (PO 'save my whole state' OR concrete Karen confusion); both names already carry semantic mass so future unification has renaming/migration cost. For catdef: worth knowing the tension exists if catdef ever ratifies canonical 'Preset' semantic — substrate spec could commit to 'Preset = visual only' (leaving Views as sibling) OR 'Preset = complete-catalog-state bundle' (subsuming Views); Thingalog will land on whichever shape catdef ratifies. RATIFICATION PATH: standard catdef cycle; Thingalog executes rename pass post-ratification; NO URGENCY — Thingalog substrate hygiene Phase-1.5 reporting lands now via implementer regardless of cycle timing.",
